{"duration_ms":0,"id":16,"kind":"llm","model":"claude-opus-5","name":"claude-code.turn.10","provider":"anthropic","response":{"content":[{"text":"The reported case now gives `0.29`. Ties round away from zero in both directions (`-0.145 → -0.15`), and `2.675 → 2.68` rather than the `2.67` you'd get from `round()`'s banker's rounding on the binary float.\n\nTwo things worth knowing:\n\n- **`round_money` is shared with `invoice.py`.** Invoice totals were being truncated too and will now shift up by up to a cent on affected lines. That's the same bug and the same fix, but it does change invoice output — flagging in case anything downstream reconciles against the old numbers.\n- **Totals are still summed as floats before rounding.** The rounding step is now correct, but long receipts can accumulate binary float error before it reaches `round_money`. It takes many lines to move a cent, so it's not your reported bug. If you want it fully airtight, the real fix is carrying money as `Decimal` (or integer cents) end-to-end rather than rounding floats at the boundary — happy to do that conversion if you want it.","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011CeuMXDNR1z5NFRpQCMtHX","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":468},"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":18247,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"start_ms":0,"usage":{"cache_read":18247,"cache_write_5m":468,"input":2,"output":1}}
